From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] add direct Wayland EGL presentation to host HWUI

Add a host-only RenderProxy/CanvasContext surface seam so Artzig can bind
its wl_display and wl_surface directly. The Ganesh pipeline now owns a
Wayland EGL window surface and presents with eglSwapBuffers, eliminating
the per-frame GPU readback, Java Bitmap copy, and wl_shm upload.

Also provide real GPU-backed host hardware bitmaps, render-thread uploads
and readback, initialize DeviceInfo from the live Ganesh context, and make
the optional ActivityManager RenderThread scheduling notification tolerate
host runtimes without a system server.

Report the actual nested resource chunk type in LoadedArsc diagnostics so
host resource-table incompatibilities can be identified accurately.
